## Isolation Model

```text
┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────────┐
│  django/ │  │ flutter/ │  │  react/  │  │  vuejs/  │  │  wordpress/  │
│ AGENTS   │  │ AGENTS   │  │ AGENTS   │  │ AGENTS   │  │   AGENTS     │
│ agents/  │  │ agents/  │  │ agents/  │  │ agents/  │  │   agents/    │
│ skills/  │  │ skills/  │  │ skills/  │  │ skills/  │  │   skills/    │
│ arch_pl/ │  │ arch_pl/ │  │ arch_pl/ │  │ arch_pl/ │  │   arch_pl/   │
└──────────┘  └──────────┘  └──────────┘  └──────────┘  └──────────────┘
     ╳              ╳              ╳              ╳              ╳
ZERO cross-links between any frameworks. Ship any single directory.
```

Universal rules (git safety, simplicity, planning workflow, etc.) are embedded **inside** each framework as framework-specific skills (`<fw>-code-standards/`, `<fw>-implementation-planning/`, etc.) — tailored to that framework's commands, tools, and conventions.

